
 viewordusage - Report Order data usage.

 Queries the 'ousage' table in PostgreSQL database 'rdadb' and produces
 an order usage view/report grouped and filtered by the options you choose.

 USAGE:
   viewordusage [-C] ColumnNames [-O OrderColumnNames]
                <one or more condition options>
                [output and miscellaneous options]
                [> OutputFile] [| lp -d PrinterName]

 BASIC RULES:

   1. -C ColumnNames is required (see COLUMN OPTIONS below).
      The '-C' flag may be omitted if ColumnNames is the first argument.

   2. At least one condition option must be given:
        -a -c -d -D -e -g -i -j -k -l -m -M -n -o -s -S -t -T -u -v -y

   3. Negation: for any condition option except -a, prepend '!' between
      the flag and value to invert the filter, e.g. '-o ! DSS'.

   4. Wildcards: condition options that take strings (-c, -e, -g, -i, -j,
      -k, -l, -n, -o, -S, -t, -u, -v) accept SQL wildcards '%' (any chars)
      and '_' (one char).

   5. By default the output is paginated with a header, footer, and
      column titles. Use -w for plain output (no header/totals).


 COLUMN OPTIONS:

   -C ColumnNames
        A string of one or more column letters listed below. The display
        order of columns matches their order in the string. At least one
        group column or summary column is required.

   -O OrderColumnNames
        Sort the output. Each letter must also appear in -C.
        UPPERCASE = ascending, lowercase = descending.

   Column letters:

     Group Columns:
       D* - DATE       - YYYY-MM-DD (e.g. 2004-04-25)
       E* - EMAIL      - user email address
       G* - ORGNAME    - organization name
       I* - FIRSTNAME  - user first name
       J  - PROJECT    - project id (e.g. icoads, era40, tigge)
       K  - REGION     - user region name
       L* - LASTNAME   - user last name
       M* - MONTH      - YYYY-MM (e.g. 2004-04)
       N* - ORDERNO    - order number
       O* - ORGTYPE    - organization type (DSS, NCAR, UNIV, OTHER)
       P  - PROCESSBY  - login name of the specialist who owns the order
       Q* - COUNTRY    - user country name
       R* - DSTITLE    - dataset title
       S* - OUTSIZE    - requested data size in MB
       T* - DATASET    - format dsnnn.n (e.g. d540001)
       W* - METHOD     - delivery method (ftp, tape, etc.)
       Y* - YEAR       - YYYY

       (*) = column may be displayed with zero usages when -z is used.

     Summary Columns:
       A - DSCOUNT    - number of datasets in the group
       B - MBOUTPUT   - data size (MB) requested by the group
       C - #UNIQUSER  - number of unique users in the group
       F - MBINPUT    - input data size (MB) for the group
       H - #ORDER     - number of orders in the group
       Z - COST($)    - data cost in dollars by the group

     Index Column:
       X - INDEX      - 1-based row index (use as the first column)


 CONDITION OPTIONS:

   -a   All records in 'ousage'.
   -A RowLimit                       Limit the number of rows returned.
   -c CountryCodes                   Users from these countries.
   -d DateList                       Orders on these dates (YYYY-MM-DD).
   -D StartDate [EndDate]            Orders between two dates.
   -e EMailList                      Orders by users with these emails.
   -E StartDate [EndDate]            Orders by users notified of dataset
                                     updates between these dates.
   -g OrgNames                       Users from these organization names.
   -h                                Pair with -e to include historical
                                     emails users registered with.
   -i FirstNameList                  Users with these first names.
   -j Projects                       Orders for these projects.
   -k RegionNames                    Users from these regions.
   -l LastNameList                   Users with these last names.
   -m MonthList                      Orders in these months (YYYY-MM).
   -M MethodList                     Orders via these delivery methods.
   -n OrderNumberList                Orders with these order numbers.
   -o OrgTypes                       Users from these org types.
                                     Default: '-o ! DSS' (excludes DSS).
                                     Use '-o ALL' to include every type.
   -s MinSize [MaxSize]              Output data sizes in MB in this range.
   -S SpecialistLoginNames           Specialists who own the orders.
   -t DatasetList                    Orders for these datasets.
   -T MinDataset [MaxDataset]        Orders for datasets in this ID range,
                                     e.g. '-T d540000 d550009'.
   -u ProcessSpecialists             Orders processed by these specialists.
   -v OrderNumbers                   Orders matching these order numbers.
   -y YearList                       Orders in these years (YYYY).


 OUTPUT AND MISCELLANEOUS OPTIONS:

   -H Title           Replace the default report title.
   -L Delimiter       Use Delimiter between columns instead of spaces.
   -U SizeUnit        Show sizes in unit: B, K, M, or G.
   -w                 Simple format: no header, no totals.
   -z                 Include users and/or datasets without usage.
   > OutputFile       Redirect output to a file.
   | lp -d Printer    Send output to the named printer (e.g. lj100).


 EXAMPLES:

   View annual order usage in 2005 with columns INDEX, EMAIL, ORGTYPE,
   #ORDER, MBOUTPUT; sort by ORGTYPE ascending and MBOUTPUT descending:

      viewordusage XEOHB -y 2005 -O Ob

   Same, excluding DSS users, and save to a file:

      viewordusage XEOHB -y 2005 -o ! DSS -O Ob > ordusage.out
